WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.980
Umm, Yunoki-sempai. I'm going to try to give it my all.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.610
Thank you for worrying about me.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.800
Worry?

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.450
Me... about <i>you</i>?

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.160
You didn't know, did you?

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.090
You're annoying.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:11.060
The Pianissimo of Guilt

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.450
Sheesh, it's hard when people just don't get it.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.870
I'm telling you to withdraw from the competition.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.630
As you are right now you'll only mess up the next selection for everyone.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:37.130
The bar will be raised for the next selection... You'll only end up embarrassing yourself.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.630
Don't worry.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:45.010
Nobody will care if you're not there anymore.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:47.470
You know this to be true.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.440
Right, Hino?

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.860
You'll put her in a tough spot.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.580
I'm Yunoki Azuma.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.290
I have to help her.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.470
Kaho-chan, what's the matter?

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:18.710
You don't look so good.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.810
Welcome home, Kahoko.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:34.770
Hey, Kahoko! Not even going to answer your mother?

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:39.690
So, don't overdo it Hino-san.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.170
Why?

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.080
You're annoying.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.750
What in the world was that?

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.490
Hey, Kaho-chan...

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.000
Did something happen?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.170
You've been acting strange since yesterday.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.890
Um, you see.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:13.520
Actually... You see, it's about Yunoki-sempai from the Music Department.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.060
I heard Yunoki-sempai is a Gemini!

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.070
That's a good match for an Aquarius like me!

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:23.570
Yunoki-sempai really is great! I look up to him.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.070
I can't tell her.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.300
So, what about Yunoki-sempai, Kaho-chan?

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:33.040
No, never mind.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.680
What's the matter?

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.250
Amo-san.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:53.270
You were sighing. Are you tired from practicing so much?

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.750
Um, you see, it's about Yunoki-sempai.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:01.440
Hino-san.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:08.820
Oww...

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.260
You all right?

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.590
Are you OK?

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:17.050
Yes, I am fine.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.790
I can stand up by myself.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.010
Hino-san, your knee...

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.850
We have to wash out the wound quickly.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.460
Come here, Hino-san.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.260
W-Wait a second!

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.440
What was that?

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.170
Thank you very much, Yunoki-sempai.

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:45.690
No problem. Does it hurt?

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:48.650
No.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.990
Good, I'm glad.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:59.490
I guess you were thinking about what I said to you, Hino.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:05.520
About whether you really feel you should withdraw from the competition or not.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:10.550
Um, I've decided to do my best.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:14.310
So I'm not going to quit after only coming halfway.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.160
I see.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:17.730
Yes?

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:22.390
That's some guts you got there, Hino.

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:24.290
Makes me want to tease you.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:30.100
And are you OK like this?

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:33.660
What if I told everyone the kinds of things you say to me?

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:37.370
So you even have the nerve to do that?

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:38.770
But...

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.830
Aren't you just deceiving everyone?

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:45.540
Deceive? That doesn't sound very refined.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:48.300
Don't you think that'll cause trouble for someone?

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.260
Or perhaps...

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.240
Yunoki-sempai!

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:07.150
Just a little joke.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:12.110
Even if you ran away from here and tried to find someone to help,

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:15.650
who would everyone believe?

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:20.060
Me, the perfect honor student trusted throughout the school,

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:23.290
or you, a single student from General Studies?

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:27.500
It's pointless no matter what you say.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:31.180
And anyway, everyone has a secret or two.

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:37.430
Are you saying you're willing to lay yourself out completely bare?

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.110
Kaho-chan, practicing again today?

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:53.830
Good luck.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:57.870
Thank you.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:06.360
Are you saying you're willing to lay yourself out completely bare?

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.340
I can't do that.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.720
Because I'm actually...

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:15.480
That is a magical violin. Anyone can play it.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:22.540
I'm the one who's been deceiving everybody.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:27.410
I have no right to criticize Yunoki-sempai.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:29.800
Hey.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.350
Practicing?

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.000
Yeah.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.880
What's the matter? Did something happen?

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:40.580
No, nothing in particular.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:46.790
Do you remember what I told you before?

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:53.320
If you're troubled by something, come talk to me, your fellow General Studies student.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.300
Right.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.750
You can tell me. Anytime.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.760
Thank you, Tsuchiura-kun.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:03.690
OK, see you tomorrow.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.830
Thank you.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:09.630
But, I can't tell you.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:32.930
Stroking this part correctly is difficult.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:39.600
I have to follow what the composer intended by what is written in the score.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.770
But I have a feeling that there's something missing.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.950
I wonder what that is?

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:57.740
Shimizu-kun only ever thinks about music.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:14.300
Fuyuumi-chan said that she wants to be like me.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:23.510
I'm deceiving everyone! Lying to everyone!

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:32.160
Going home already?

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.240
Yeah.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.740
That's quite early of you.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.200
What happened to your knee?

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:43.450
I kinda fell on the stairs.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:47.870
But it's nothing serious, just a scratch.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:52.010
You don't take proper precautions. What if you hurt your fingers again?

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:54.060
It's almost time for the third selection.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.210
That's true.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:11:03.180
Since you got second place last time, the focus is going to be all the more on you.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.780
It's obvious you'll be under pressure.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:11.910
But you can't use that pressure to push aside your practice.

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:13.390
Tsukimori-kun.

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:15.860
I have to practice, if you'll excuse me.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:32.540
Oh?

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:40.590
What's this? Hino looks really down and out.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.240
Your ash is about to fall, Kanazawa-sensei.

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:47.810
Hello.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.360
So, what are you looking at?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.900
That girl... The one from the competition?

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:00.860
Hino-chan!

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:03.360
Hihara-sempai!

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:07.920
Going home already?

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:10.790
Yes. And you, Sempai?

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.040
Nope. I'm going to orchestra practice now.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:17.590
It sounds like fun, yeah.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:18.920
Of course!

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:21.710
Hey, Hino-chan, why don't you come?

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.220
Yeah, why not?

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:26.790
No, I...

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:29.220
I'm really not in the mood for that now.

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:31.410
I'll introduce you to everybody!

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:32.060
But...

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:34.650
I'll be really happy if you came, Hino-chan.

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:39.820
Oh, Yunoki!

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:43.970
Now, now, Hihara. Making trouble for Hino-san?

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:46.780
That's it! Why don't you come too, Yunoki?

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:51.110
See, Hino-chan, it'll be even better with two or three people.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.580
You want to take me with you?

00:12:55.990 --> 00:13:01.420
It is true that it'd be better than going to some club as an outsider by myself.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:04.660
No, actually with Yunoki-sempai it'd be more like...

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:07.440
Yunoki-sama!

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:09.210
He'll just overshadow me completely!

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.430
Sure, I'll come with you!

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:18.110
So, you're spreading the pain, I see.

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:19.860
All right!

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:24.740
Yo!

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:26.450
Hihara-sempai!

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:28.760
Kazuki, you're late!

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:30.280
Sorry about that!

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.040
It's been a long time, Hihara-sempai.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:37.290
Good work, everyone.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.510
That's Yunoki-sempai for you.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:45.800
A real superstar.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:50.760
Hino-san?

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:54.730
It is! It's Hino-san!

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.520
I-I'm sorry!

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.390
What are you apologizing for?

00:13:59.390 --> 00:14:00.480
But...

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.770
Your performance the other day was wonderful!

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:05.880
You should have joined the Music Department.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.950
How long have you been playing the violin?

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:10.040
Hey, try asking her.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:11.300
Is it OK?

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:13.000
But I'm interested.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.050
Hino-san.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:18.500
Is it true you're going out with Tsuchiura-kun?

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:20.950
Is that true?

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:23.280
That's the rumor, anyway.

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:25.220
You know what happened back at the first selection, right?

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:26.510
So, what about it?

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.340
Going out?!

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:30.490
Uh, n-no...

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:31.050
No!

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:34.120
Kaho-chan and Tsuchiura aren't like that!

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:36.480
Tsuchiura told me himself.

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:41.900
It's true, I haven't heard anything myself about that.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:48.940
By the way, where should I practice my flute?

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:52.160
Since I'm here, I thought I would join you.

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:55.090
Thank you so much for your help!

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:59.570
That's our Yunoki for you. He changed the conversation just like that.

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:01.460
Sorry about that, Hino-chan.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.350
Oh, please don't worry about it.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:05.550
Hino-sempai!

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.220
Yes?

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:11.470
She's so cute! Is she a first year?

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:16.850
You see, at the next beginners' recital I have a solo part.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:21.020
I'd love it if you could listen to me play and give me some advice.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.140
Me?

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:27.780
Yes. I'm sorry for asking you just like this.

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:30.360
But I can't...

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.260
Why not?

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:33.450
Go ahead and play.

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.910
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.780
You can do it, Mai.

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:38.710
Right.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:40.600
But, I...

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:42.670
What should I do?

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:54.480
She's good.

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:08.320
Um, how was it?

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.530
It was really great!

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.530
She didn't ask <i>you</i>.

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.850
It seems the more I play, the more I keep going around in circles.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:19.150
What are you talking about? You're really working hard, Mai.

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:20.500
You can play it all fine.

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:24.400
Everyone... Everyone is working so hard.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:25.700
And yet, I...

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.250
I'm sorry.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:32.120
I have no right to give you any advice.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:34.480
I'm sorry.

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:37.140
Hino-chan!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:50.190
Hino-chan!

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:51.910
What's the matter?

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:53.860
Um...

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.930
Can you continue on with the rehearsal for me?

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:00.270
I'll be right back.

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.190
What's the matter with Hino-chan?

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:10.560
You really have taken an interest in Hino-san, haven't you, Hihara?

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:12.710
I-I haven't really...

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:13.970
Yes, you have.

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:18.260
Stop teasing me.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:20.550
Sorry.

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:26.060
It was shocking.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:30.690
That time when he was playing all by himself on stage.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:33.800
The pride Tsukimori-kun had for that stage.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.200
Those strong feelings that are about to crumble at any moment...

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:51.030
Compared to that, I'm nothing.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.220
Hino-san.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:59.390
Thank goodness, I caught up to you.

00:18:02.550 --> 00:18:03.730
When did I...

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:06.390
It's the person who was playing the violin for those children.

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.700
I'm Shinobu Osaki.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:14.190
I'm an alumni here and I help out with the Orchestra club.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.630
Osaki-san.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:19.530
Oh, you're the person who volunteers to help the Orchestra club!

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.000
Oh, s-sorry!

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:24.700
Don't worry.

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:28.240
That's something that Kanazawa-sensei said, right?

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:30.300
It sounds like something he'd say.

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:37.680
That's right. He said that he majored in violin and won the grand prize in the competition.

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:42.580
I really enjoyed your performances during the competition, Hino-san.

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.550
Congratulations on getting second place last time.

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.590
I-It wasn't really...

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:51.110
I still think it's strange that I'm even participating.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:52.350
Why?

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:57.000
I think that having a General Studies student like yourself participating means a lot.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:01.130
Because with you participating,

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:06.000
a lot of people who didn't care about music before are now interested in the competition.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:09.710
Don't you think that's amazing?

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:15.420
Back when I participated, the people in General Studies didn't really pay much attention.

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:19.740
So, I think it's pretty amazing.

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:24.230
I feel relieved when I'm around this person.

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:26.400
Osaki-sempai.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:31.680
Can I hear you play your violin, Osaki-sempai?

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:33.670
Right now, here?

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.900
I-I'm sorry, that's asking too much, isn't it?

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:40.560
What am I saying?

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:41.540
Sure.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.700
Although I can't play anything much, really.

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:49.210
Do you have a request?

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:52.700
Um... Whatever you'd like!

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:58.300
Ah, then hmm, how about Debussy's "Beau Soir?"

00:19:58.300 --> 00:19:59.960
Soir?

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:05.250
I think it's normal for everyone to have changing feelings about the competition.

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.640
But the important things are always the same.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:14.480
I just want everyone to enjoy my playing. That's all.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.730
It sounds so kind...

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:05.540
I've just been thinking about myself this whole time.

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:10.160
I wasn't thinking about how much I hurt those around me, and I wasn't being kind.

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:13.640
I have to apologize to that girl from before.

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:18.820
I have to tell her how surprised I was at her wonderful performance.

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:33.460
It's a melody like a beautiful sunset.

00:21:34.510 --> 00:21:37.150
It warms me to the bottom of my heart.

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:39.050
I'm so relieved.

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:43.950
It's like the sound is gently embracing me.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.980
Such a kind sound...

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:40.310
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:40.310 --> 00:23:44.700
The orchestra began as the accompaniment for opera in the 16th century.

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:50.170
Starting in the 19th century, a number of great symphonies were composed one after another,

00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:53.740
and in the present day it has developed into one of the most important musical ensembles.

00:23:55.310 --> 00:23:57.440
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:57.440 --> 00:24:04.750
Mahler's Symphony No. 8 requires such a large orchestra, what do they call the ensemble?

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:06.980
I forgot!

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:08.380
It's almost time for midterms!

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:12.180
